{:edb/db-before-t 1228 :edb/db-after-t 1229 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534541 50 #inst "2026-10-12T02:26:44.916Z" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186052917 1075 #edb/ref 17592186052918 13194139534541 17592186045417 false] [17592186052917 1075 #edb/ref 17592186052921 13194139534541 17592186045417 false] [17592186052917 1075 #edb/ref 17592186052922 13194139534541 17592186045417 false] [17592186052917 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424929 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186052917 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424940 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186052917 1075 #edb/ref 17592186424945 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186052917 1078 #edb/ref 17592186424929 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186053577 1078 #edb/ref 17592186053580 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054421 1071 "Which of the following is a variable?\n\n1. $x$\n2. $x+1$\n3. $1$\n4. $x+1=2$" 13194139534541 17592186045417 false] [17592186054421 1071 "Which of the following is a variable?\n\nI. $x$\n\nII. $x+1$\n\nIII. $1$\n\nIV. $x+1=2$" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054421 1074 "Let's look at each one in turn.\n\n1. $x$ is a variable because it's a single letter by itself.\n2. $x+1$ is an algebraic expression, not a variable.\n3. $1$ is a number, not a variable.\n4. $x+1=2$ contains an equals sign $(=)$ and is an **equation**, not a variable. You'll learn more about equations later.\n\nSo, only choice I represents a variable." 13194139534541 17592186045417 false] [17592186054421 1074 "Let's look at each one in turn.\n\nI. $x$ is a variable because it's a single letter by itself.\n\nII. $x+1$ is an algebraic expression, not a variable.\n\nIII. $1$ is a number, not a variable.\n\nIV. $x+1=2$ contains an equals sign $(=)$ and is an **equation**, not a variable. You'll learn more about equations later.\n\nSo, only choice I represents a variable." 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054422 1074 "If we denote our number by $x$, then \"the sum of three and a number\" can be written as \n\n$$\n3+x.\n$$\n\n**Note:** There are other correct answers as well. We could choose another letter, such as $a$, to represent the number. In that case, \"the sum of three and a number\" could also be written as \n\n$$\n3+a.\n$$" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054422 1074 "If we denote our number by $x$, then \"the sum of three and a number\" can be written as $3+x$.\n\n**Note:** There are other correct answers as well. We could choose another letter, such as $a$, to represent the number. In that case, \"the sum of three and a number\" could also be written as $3+a$." 13194139534541 17592186045417 false] [17592186054423 1074 "If we denote our number by $x$, then \"the difference of eight and a number\" can be written as \n\n$$\n8-x.\n$$" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054423 1074 "If we denote our number by $x$, then \"the difference of eight and a number\" can be written as $8-x$." 13194139534541 17592186045417 false] [17592186054799 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424970 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054799 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424974 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054799 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424978 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054799 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424982 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054800 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424971 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054800 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424972 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054800 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424976 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054800 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424979 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054800 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424981 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054801 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424973 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054801 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424975 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054801 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424977 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054801 1038 #edb/ref 17592186424980 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186054915 1050 420.0 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186055280 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186055280 1074 "If we denote our number by $q$, then the phrase can be written as\n\n$$\nq-22.\n$$" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186055390 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186055390 1071 "Which of the following is a variable?\n\n1. $h$\n2. $k - 2$\n3. $3$" 13194139534541 17592186045417 false] [17592186055390 1071 "Which of the following is a variable?\n\nI. $h$\n\nII. $k-2$\n\nIII. $3$" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186055390 1074 "Let's look at each one in turn.\n\nI. $h$ is a variable because it's a single letter by itself.\n\nII. $k-2$ is an algebraic expression, not a variable.\n\nIII. $3$ is a number, not a variable.\n\nSo, only choice I represents a variable." 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186056032 1064 "A **variable** is any letter or symbol that can be replaced by a number. For example, the letters\n\n$$\nx, \\quad y, \\quad z, \\quad a, \\quad b, \\quad c, \\quad k, \\quad m,\\quad n,\\quad p, \\quad q,\\quad r, \\quad \\ldots\n$$\n\nare commonly used as variables. But in general, we can use any letter we like.\n\nAn **algebraic expression** is a combination of variables with mathematical operations, like addition $(+)$, subtraction $(-)$, multiplication $(\\times)$, and division $(\\div).$ So \n\n$$\nx+2,\\qquad 6-y,\\qquad 2\\times p + 1,\\qquad q\\div r,\n$$\n\nare all examples of algebraic expressions." 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186056032 1064 "A **variable** is any letter or symbol that can be replaced by a number. For example, the letters\n$x, \\quad y, \\quad z, \\quad a, \\quad b, \\quad c, \\quad k, \\quad m,\\quad n,\\quad p, \\quad q,\\quad r, \\quad \\ldots$\n\nare commonly used as variables. But in general, we can use any letter we like.\n\nAn **algebraic expression** is a combination of variables with mathematical operations, like addition $(+)$, subtraction $(-)$, multiplication $(\\times)$, and division $(\\div)$. So\n$x+2,\\qquad 6-y,\\qquad 2\\times p + 1,\\qquad q\\div r$,\nare all examples of algebraic expressions." 13194139534541 17592186045417 false] [17592186424905 1080 "1" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424905 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424905 1083 #uuid "065d61d0-5556-5074-9e29-24c4baf0b670" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424906 1080 "x-15" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424906 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424906 1083 #uuid "06d2caf5-2ca8-516b-9a32-f519f23e90e6" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424907 1080 "z+13" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424907 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424907 1083 #uuid "087fab48-9c1b-5aa5-9c2b-01e2d73f785f" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424908 1080 "25-a" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424908 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424908 1083 #uuid "129b3c03-220f-51f0-99e1-7a0dfa68f672" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424909 1080 "35+q" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424909 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424909 1083 #uuid "134b8ab6-560d-5ac1-b6a1-78f429eefdfc" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424910 1080 "25a" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424910 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424910 1083 #uuid "23f6801b-e089-53af-9116-cc93c3cdd9d0" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424911 1080 "II only" 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424911 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045499 13194139534541 17592186045417 true] [17592186424911 1083 #uuid "289c50a0-ecfe-528e-8457-52cef5a9eea4" 1319